Right $\triangle ABC$ has $AB=3$, $BC=4$, and $AC=5$.  Square $XYZW$ is inscribed in $\triangle ABC$ with $X$ and $Y$ on $\overline{AC}$, $W$ on $\overline{AB}$, and $Z$ on $\overline{BC}$.  What is the side length of the square?

[asy]
pair A,B,C,W,X,Y,Z;
A=(-9,0); B=(0,12); C=(16,0);
W=(12A+25B)/37;
Z =(12C+25B)/37;
X=foot(W,A,C);
Y=foot(Z,A,C);
draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(X--W--Z--Y);
label("$A$",A,SW);
label("$B$",B,N);
label("$C$",C,E);
label("$W$",W,NW);
label("$X$",X,S);
label("$Y$",Y,S);
label("$Z$",Z,NE);
[/asy]

An acute isosceles triangle, $ABC$, is inscribed in a circle.  Through $B$ and $C$, tangents to the circle are drawn, meeting at point $D$.  If $\angle ABC = \angle ACB = 2 \angle D$ and $\angle BAC = k \pi$ in radians, then find $k$.

[asy]
import graph;

unitsize(2 cm);

pair O, A, B, C, D;

O = (0,0);
A = dir(90);
B = dir(-30);
C = dir(210);
D = extension(B, B + rotate(90)*(B), C, C + rotate(90)*(C));

draw(Circle(O,1));
draw(A--B--C--cycle);
draw(B--D--C);

label("$A$", A, N);
label("$B$", B, SE);
label("$C$", C, SW);
label("$D$", D, S);
[/asy]

